way into the Cloud of today.

00:06:12.410 --> 00:06:15.440
For sure, what I
have taken forward,

00:06:15.440 --> 00:06:19.450
is the passion for Cloud.

00:06:19.450 --> 00:06:22.900
And I'm quite sure it's
this passion for Cloud that

00:06:22.900 --> 00:06:25.760
has brought me here today.

00:06:25.760 --> 00:06:28.990
My name is Michael
Korbacher, and I'm

00:06:28.990 --> 00:06:33.560
running Google's Cloud
business for Germany, Austria,

00:06:33.560 --> 00:06:36.790
and Switzerland.

00:06:36.790 --> 00:06:40.710
Now, the time has
not stood still,

00:06:40.710 --> 00:06:45.740
and Google has progressed
and we have progressed.

00:06:45.740 --> 00:06:50.000
And if we look at from
what happened something

00:06:50.000 --> 00:06:54.440
like 19 years ago in a
garage in the Silicon Valley

00:06:54.440 --> 00:06:58.000
where people started pulling
together infrastructure held

00:06:58.000 --> 00:07:01.450
together with LEGO
blocks, we're now

00:07:01.450 --> 00:07:04.450
looking at an
infrastructure where

00:07:04.450 --> 00:07:06.760
we're running numerous
services that have,

00:07:06.760 --> 00:07:11.240
on a regular basis, more
than a billion users.

00:07:11.240 --> 00:07:13.890
Think about Gmail.

00:07:13.890 --> 00:07:15.630
Think about YouTube.

00:07:15.630 --> 00:07:16.590
Think about Search.

00:07:16.590 --> 00:07:17.490
Think about Maps.

00:07:17.490 --> 00:07:21.030
Think about Play,
Android, and so on.

00:07:21.030 --> 00:07:24.950
What an infrastructure it takes.

00:07:24.950 --> 00:07:30.500
And all that based on
an idea and a mission

00:07:30.500 --> 00:07:34.520
that I would call
rather ambitious.

00:07:34.520 --> 00:07:37.510
A mission that said
in a simple form,

00:07:37.510 --> 00:07:42.060
well, we're going to
take the internet.

00:07:42.060 --> 00:07:44.780
We're going to
index the internet.

00:07:44.780 --> 00:07:49.040
We let people search that
index, and we give them

00:07:49.040 --> 00:07:53.400
relevant answers
to their searches

00:07:53.400 --> 00:07:55.740
no matter where they
are on the planet,

00:07:55.740 --> 00:07:58.680
ideally within milliseconds.

00:07:58.680 --> 00:08:01.800
That was a big ambition
when you think about it,

00:08:01.800 --> 00:08:04.660
to organize the
world's information

00:08:04.660 --> 00:08:08.970
to make it universally
accessible and useful.

00:08:08.970 --> 00:08:10.530
That's a very big
ambition when you

00:08:10.530 --> 00:08:13.500
think about how the
internet evolved

00:08:13.500 --> 00:08:16.350
and how the internet grew.

00:08:16.350 --> 00:08:18.570
To make that happen,
there was probably

00:08:18.570 --> 00:08:23.490
not a lot of off the
shelf products that would

00:08:23.490 --> 00:08:26.950
make this mission come true.

00:08:26.950 --> 00:08:27.580
Think about it.

00:08:27.580 --> 00:08:31.870
What file system could actually
manage that volume of data

00:08:31.870 --> 00:08:34.210
that you would create?

00:08:34.210 --> 00:08:37.390
What networking gear
could actually handle

00:08:37.390 --> 00:08:38.665
all this bandwidth required?

00:08:41.890 --> 00:08:44.830
What product would
I use to search

00:08:44.830 --> 00:08:48.850
this amount of unstructured
data and give people

00:08:48.850 --> 00:08:52.270
replies within milliseconds?

00:08:52.270 --> 00:08:54.650
How do I scale?

00:08:54.650 --> 00:08:57.820
How do I scale out?

00:08:57.820 --> 00:09:02.200
And how do I improve my
results using technologies

00:09:02.200 --> 00:09:07.630
like machine learning or
artificial intelligence?

00:09:07.630 --> 00:09:13.150
So when looking at this to
get to where we are today,

00:09:13.150 --> 00:09:17.880
one of the requirements was
to drive constant innovation,

00:09:17.880 --> 00:09:21.750
to explore a path that
nobody has gone before.

00:09:21.750 --> 00:09:24.090
And that led to the
development of things

00:09:24.090 --> 00:09:27.670
like the Google File System.

00:09:27.670 --> 00:09:29.260
When we're talking
about BigQuery,

00:09:29.260 --> 00:09:34.110
how do we search large
amounts of unstructured data?

00:09:34.110 --> 00:09:39.090
When we think about developments
such as Kubernetes, container

00:09:39.090 --> 00:09:42.000
based technologies, how
do we distribute workloads

00:09:42.000 --> 00:09:46.330
across servers, data
centers, Clouds,

00:09:46.330 --> 00:09:53.180
as well as making machine
learning more accessible,

00:09:53.180 --> 00:09:56.300
and artificial intelligence
more accessible,

00:09:56.300 --> 00:10:01.150
through frameworks
like TensorFlow?

00:10:01.150 --> 00:10:03.850
Now the great news
is, in necessity

00:10:03.850 --> 00:10:07.540
of fulfilling our mission, we've
created all this innovation,

00:10:07.540 --> 00:10:13.620
and we've given it back to
the open source community.

00:10:13.620 --> 00:10:19.170
And now we're taking all
this, the infrastructure that

00:10:19.170 --> 00:10:24.090
serves billions, and the
tools that run Google,

00:10:24.090 --> 00:10:28.170
and we're making this
available to companies

00:10:28.170 --> 00:10:29.760
in the form of Google Cloud.

00:10:34.200 --> 00:10:38.720
You might think, hm,
all right, that's great.

00:10:38.720 --> 00:10:39.580
I'm a manufacturer.

00:10:39.580 --> 00:10:41.240
I'm a retailer.

00:10:41.240 --> 00:10:44.750
I'm a logistics
company, or I'm a bank.

00:10:44.750 --> 00:10:45.455
Why do I care?

00:10:50.160 --> 00:10:58.690
Well, you should care because if
you are a traditional company,

00:10:58.690 --> 00:11:02.290
what sets you apart in
the past, which might be,

00:11:02.290 --> 00:11:05.480
oh, I've got a big data center.

00:11:05.480 --> 00:11:09.320
And in that big data center, I
run some really big enterprise

00:11:09.320 --> 00:11:10.940
IT.

00:11:10.940 --> 00:11:13.470
I might have been your
competitive advantage

00:11:13.470 --> 00:11:15.310
in the past.

00:11:15.310 --> 00:11:21.770
For some of you, this might
be a slight burden today

00:11:21.770 --> 00:11:24.290
because one of the key
things that companies

00:11:24.290 --> 00:11:28.760
need to be aware of, and that
maybe is your treasure, not

00:11:28.760 --> 00:11:33.440
your data center, but the
data within that data center.

00:11:33.440 --> 00:11:35.240
And how do you exploit?

00:11:35.240 --> 00:11:36.510
How do you use?

00:11:36.510 --> 00:11:40.610
How do you make better decision
from that data within your data

00:11:40.610 --> 00:11:43.450
center?

00:11:43.450 --> 00:11:47.210
And that often
requires the tools

00:11:47.210 --> 00:11:51.770
that are available
in the public Cloud.

00:11:51.770 --> 00:11:54.140
I don't think your
sense of urgency

00:11:54.140 --> 00:12:01.340
is to take a workload from A to
B and then save 20% on the way,

00:12:01.340 --> 00:12:03.380
or you name it.

00:12:03.380 --> 00:12:07.130
That does not necessarily
imply a sense of urgency,

00:12:07.130 --> 00:12:09.860
especially if you
think about companies

00:12:09.860 --> 00:12:14.550
doing quite well as an
average across the region.

00:12:14.550 --> 00:12:16.950
Your sense of urgency
is a different one.

00:12:16.950 --> 00:12:19.590
You want to be prepared
for the future.

00:12:19.590 --> 00:12:24.330
And you want to be using the
tools that your competition can

00:12:24.330 --> 00:12:25.260
use as well.

00:12:25.260 --> 00:12:27.930
And your competition
might be somebody

00:12:27.930 --> 00:12:30.270
that you have not been
dealing with in the past.

00:12:30.270 --> 00:12:33.060
That might be that
startup company

00:12:33.060 --> 00:12:38.110
that takes their credit card,
goes to the Google Cloud,

00:12:38.110 --> 00:12:42.070
registers on the portal,
goes to the console,

00:12:42.070 --> 00:12:50.800
and within 90 seconds, spawns up
a thousand node Hadoop cluster.

00:12:50.800 --> 00:12:54.190
They use it for 10 minutes,
and then it takes them

00:12:54.190 --> 00:12:57.260
60 seconds to shut it down.

00:12:57.260 --> 00:12:58.990
That is your competition today.

00:12:58.990 --> 00:13:01.150
At the end of the
month, they will

00:13:01.150 --> 00:13:03.100
find an invoice on
their credit card

00:13:03.100 --> 00:13:08.870
statement for 12 and 1/2 minutes
of usage of Google Cloud.

00:13:08.870 --> 00:13:12.570
This is the environment
that we're in today,

00:13:12.570 --> 00:13:14.540
and this is your
sense of urgency,

00:13:14.540 --> 00:13:17.690
whether you're a startup or
whether you're an established

00:13:17.690 --> 00:13:18.740
company.

00:13:18.740 --> 00:13:21.800
You want to stay ahead
of the competition.

00:13:21.800 --> 00:13:26.250
You want to do that with the
latest tools available to you.

00:13:26.250 --> 00:13:28.260
You want to look at
how you work together

00:13:28.260 --> 00:13:31.040
and be more collaborative.

00:13:31.040 --> 00:13:35.440
Increasing productivity
is everybody's challenge.

00:13:35.440 --> 00:13:38.320
You want to be, at
the end of today,

00:13:38.320 --> 00:13:42.820
more agile, more
reactive to changes

00:13:42.820 --> 00:13:46.680
in the business, ideally you
want to be proactive, really.

00:13:50.390 --> 00:13:54.170
And all that as you're
dealing with security threats

00:13:54.170 --> 00:13:56.330
out there on the
internet, you want

00:13:56.330 --> 00:13:59.840
to do all that, ideally,
and be more safe.

00:13:59.840 --> 00:14:06.240
And this is where Google
and the Cloud can help.

00:14:06.240 --> 00:14:11.210
For us, this region, Germany,
Austria, and Switzerland,

00:14:11.210 --> 00:14:14.940
is one of the key
regions on the planet.

00:14:14.940 --> 00:14:17.820
It's a center of innovation.

00:14:17.820 --> 00:14:21.500
It's the home of many
multinational companies

00:14:21.500 --> 00:14:25.500
that have global influence.

00:14:25.500 --> 00:14:28.760
And this investment that we're
making, and this importance,

00:14:28.760 --> 00:14:31.660
is reflected by the
investments we're making.

00:14:31.660 --> 00:14:35.120
And one of the investments
we've announced three months ago

00:14:35.120 --> 00:14:37.700
is local computing power.

00:14:37.700 --> 00:14:41.450
It is our data
region in Frankfurt,

00:14:41.450 --> 00:14:44.000
which has dramatically
reduced the latency

00:14:44.000 --> 00:14:47.660
and opens up new opportunities
for application development

00:14:47.660 --> 00:14:50.810
and application deployment
within the region.

00:14:50.810 --> 00:14:54.770
And it helps companies to keep
their applications and data

00:14:54.770 --> 00:14:57.000
close to their heart.

00:14:57.000 --> 00:15:00.620
We're completely
committed to GDPR.

00:15:00.620 --> 00:15:04.040
Who's busy with GDPR at this
point in time, the General Data

00:15:04.040 --> 00:15:06.220
Protection Regulation?

00:15:06.220 --> 00:15:06.800
Many.

00:15:06.800 --> 00:15:08.210
So are we.

00:15:08.210 --> 00:15:11.160
And we think this is a blessing.

00:15:11.160 --> 00:15:14.960
So we're taking what used to
be a guidance from the European

00:15:14.960 --> 00:15:17.750
Union, which was then
interpreted slightly

00:15:17.750 --> 00:15:20.660
differently from all
the member states--

00:15:20.660 --> 00:15:23.240
and then if you look at
the states within Germany,

00:15:23.240 --> 00:15:25.940
they might have had
their own preferences.

00:15:25.940 --> 00:15:29.780
We're taking that into a general
regulation which can help us,

00:15:29.780 --> 00:15:33.410
and which will help us, and
we're completely committed

00:15:33.410 --> 00:15:36.150
to this new regulation.

00:15:36.150 --> 00:15:38.010
Another important
thing for Germany,

00:15:38.010 --> 00:15:40.490
which has an impact
globally as well,

00:15:40.490 --> 00:15:42.980
is our partnership with SAP.

00:15:42.980 --> 00:15:44.500
We've got SAP here as well.

00:15:44.500 --> 00:15:46.670
So I'm glad to have them here.

00:15:46.670 --> 00:15:48.350
And it spawns three areas.

00:15:48.350 --> 00:15:54.070
Engineering, how we work
together to help the industry.

00:15:54.070 --> 00:16:00.310
It's running SAP's technology
on our Google Cloud Platform.

00:16:00.310 --> 00:16:05.450
As well as our partnership
around compliance,

00:16:05.450 --> 00:16:08.950
where SAP helps
our joint customers

00:16:08.950 --> 00:16:11.710
by monitoring services
and making sure

00:16:11.710 --> 00:16:14.740
that they are delivered
to the service,

00:16:14.740 --> 00:16:16.570
delivery and
quality as required.

00:16:20.350 --> 00:16:22.870
Cloud is used by many
companies across the globe.

00:16:22.870 --> 00:16:25.960
Don't worry, I'm not going to
talk about every logo here.

00:16:25.960 --> 00:16:29.050
You will know most
of these logos.

00:16:29.050 --> 00:16:31.940
And you will probably think,
gee, some of those logos,

00:16:31.940 --> 00:16:34.690
they look rather conservative,
some of those companies.

00:16:34.690 --> 00:16:38.950
I didn't know that they
were looking at Cloud.

00:16:38.950 --> 00:16:40.270
I can tell you they are.

00:16:40.270 --> 00:16:41.980
The Cloud is real.

00:16:41.980 --> 00:16:43.750
The Cloud is there.

00:16:43.750 --> 00:16:49.180
And the Cloud wouldn't be
real without our partners.

00:16:49.180 --> 00:16:50.980
Please make sure,
as you are here,

00:16:50.980 --> 00:16:54.520
to step by the partners'
booth and visit them,

00:16:54.520 --> 00:16:58.440
because they are the ones that
take your opportunities, that

00:16:58.440 --> 00:17:00.670
take your requirements,
and then make them

00:17:00.670 --> 00:17:05.150
solutions on our Cloud platform.

00:17:05.150 --> 00:17:10.880
I'm very happy to announce one
of our most prominent examples

00:17:10.880 --> 00:17:15.940
on stage, a retailer.

00:17:15.940 --> 00:17:19.869
One of the largest retailers
in Germany, needless to say,

00:17:19.869 --> 00:17:23.980
one of the largest
retailers on the planet.

00:17:23.980 --> 00:17:27.819
They serve businesses
and they serve consumers.

00:17:27.819 --> 00:17:30.490
And they have a
clear vision on how

00:17:30.490 --> 00:17:37.740
they help their customers in
their digital transformation.

00:17:37.740 --> 00:17:44.260
Please welcome on stage, the CIO
and the chief solution officer

00:17:44.260 --> 00:17:48.256
of Metro AG, Timo Salzsieder.

00:17:48.256 --> 00:17:50.240
[MUSIC PLAYING]

