clothing, books, consumer

00:19:45.490 --> 00:19:47.000
electronics, et cetera.

00:19:47.000 --> 00:19:49.450
And therefore, we
are moving obviously

00:19:49.450 --> 00:19:52.360
into the digital space now,
so the digital transformation,

00:19:52.360 --> 00:19:55.450
another buzzword used
within our organization.

00:19:55.450 --> 00:19:58.120
And due to the fact that we
have these global operations,

00:19:58.120 --> 00:20:00.790
we have obviously a couple
of massive challenges.

00:20:00.790 --> 00:20:03.580
So scalability is,
for us, critical,

00:20:03.580 --> 00:20:06.460
because we are present
in countries like India,

00:20:06.460 --> 00:20:08.830
and just imagine that you
are running some campaigns

00:20:08.830 --> 00:20:13.660
on mobile devices, send out
push messages, et cetera,

00:20:13.660 --> 00:20:15.880
which obviously means
that millions of people

00:20:15.880 --> 00:20:18.030
will approach all services.

00:20:18.030 --> 00:20:20.660
So scalability is, for
us, really important.

00:20:20.660 --> 00:20:24.640
The other issue is
performance, because we just

00:20:24.640 --> 00:20:26.170
need to make sure
that our users are

00:20:26.170 --> 00:20:29.050
getting excellent performance
out of our applications.

00:20:29.050 --> 00:20:32.200
And security, you might
have seen in the news,

00:20:32.200 --> 00:20:34.690
that Metro had also
some incidents regarding

00:20:34.690 --> 00:20:36.790
WannaCry in Russia and Ukraine.

00:20:36.790 --> 00:20:39.530
We handled it quite
easily, but at the end,

00:20:39.530 --> 00:20:42.730
we are obviously attractive
for some of the hackers.

00:20:42.730 --> 00:20:47.330
Therefore, security is
one of our top priorities.

00:20:47.330 --> 00:20:50.390
The other thing I just mentioned
is the digital business.

00:20:50.390 --> 00:20:52.400
And you see here a
couple of screenshots

00:20:52.400 --> 00:20:55.670
about our actually offering
for the digital space

00:20:55.670 --> 00:20:57.140
or classical web shops.

00:20:57.140 --> 00:21:00.020
And we implement them,
basically completely

00:21:00.020 --> 00:21:00.950
on our own solutions.

00:21:00.950 --> 00:21:03.110
That means we are not using
any external software.

00:21:03.110 --> 00:21:05.190
All of our offerings,
whether it's back

00:21:05.190 --> 00:21:08.770
end solutions or internal
solutions, and also

00:21:08.770 --> 00:21:11.900
web solutions, are implemented
with our own people.

00:21:11.900 --> 00:21:13.749
And obviously, we
have challenges

00:21:13.749 --> 00:21:15.290
like providing this
service globally.

00:21:15.290 --> 00:21:17.590
You see a nice screenshot
here of one of the apps

00:21:17.590 --> 00:21:19.190
we are running in China.

00:21:19.190 --> 00:21:22.670
On the bottom right, you see
that's one of our flagship

00:21:22.670 --> 00:21:23.570
stores in France.

00:21:23.570 --> 00:21:25.180
We have these
self-standing devices,

00:21:25.180 --> 00:21:27.090
so these little
devices on the left,

00:21:27.090 --> 00:21:30.140
and there's a kiosk system
called heavy article kiosk

00:21:30.140 --> 00:21:31.385
on the right side.

00:21:31.385 --> 00:21:33.200
And you might wonder,
why are we having

00:21:33.200 --> 00:21:35.120
a web shop within a store?

00:21:35.120 --> 00:21:36.570
So the name says it already.

00:21:36.570 --> 00:21:38.150
It's a heavy article kiosk.

00:21:38.150 --> 00:21:41.480
So if you want to order, for
example, a beer barrel, which

00:21:41.480 --> 00:21:44.040
is quite heavy, you
order it there directly.

00:21:44.040 --> 00:21:45.500
You go to the cashier.

00:21:45.500 --> 00:21:47.390
You identify yourself
with the Metro card,

00:21:47.390 --> 00:21:50.420
and then there's a nice
gentleman from our staff,

00:21:50.420 --> 00:21:53.780
and this gentleman is delivering
the beer barrel directly

00:21:53.780 --> 00:21:54.500
to your car.

00:21:54.500 --> 00:22:00.090
So this kind of service we are
offering in several stores.

00:22:00.090 --> 00:22:02.900
We are mainly driven, obviously,
by innovation, innovation

00:22:02.900 --> 00:22:04.320
about the internal services.

00:22:04.320 --> 00:22:07.040
So you see logistics
is one of the topics.

00:22:07.040 --> 00:22:08.870
The football fans
in the room might

00:22:08.870 --> 00:22:11.910
identify one of our
customers at the top right.

00:22:11.910 --> 00:22:15.030
So we are serving obviously
this football club,

00:22:15.030 --> 00:22:18.800
mostly with beer and
currywurst, and sometimes

00:22:18.800 --> 00:22:21.620
actually also with champagne,
if they play against Dortmund,

00:22:21.620 --> 00:22:23.260
mainly.

00:22:23.260 --> 00:22:26.990
And obviously, also try
to serve our customers

00:22:26.990 --> 00:22:28.830
when it comes to
actually the touch

00:22:28.830 --> 00:22:30.210
point with their customers.

00:22:30.210 --> 00:22:31.940
So for example, within
the restaurants,

00:22:31.940 --> 00:22:34.520
we will be providing
technology and service there.

00:22:34.520 --> 00:22:37.330
And the most innovative
part is on the bottom left.

00:22:37.330 --> 00:22:39.230
It's a self checkout service.

00:22:39.230 --> 00:22:42.500
And just imagine you're
having a scanning device,

00:22:42.500 --> 00:22:43.400
or it's a mobile app.

00:22:43.400 --> 00:22:47.610
You're scan in the products,
you put it into the basket,

00:22:47.610 --> 00:22:50.470
and then you drive this car
into this little device.

00:22:50.470 --> 00:22:51.330
It's a scale.

00:22:51.330 --> 00:22:53.660
So it weighs what's
in your cart.

00:22:53.660 --> 00:22:55.280
The camera is on top of it.

00:22:55.280 --> 00:22:57.100
It takes roughly
about 10 seconds.

00:22:57.100 --> 00:22:59.630
And we're doing this currently
in Poland, 10 seconds,

00:22:59.630 --> 00:23:01.010
and you're good to go.

00:23:01.010 --> 00:23:04.177
No cashier, no payment,
no credit card.

00:23:04.177 --> 00:23:04.760
It's in there.

00:23:04.760 --> 00:23:06.920
And that just gives
you an impression

00:23:06.920 --> 00:23:10.460
how innovative we
actually are doing.

00:23:10.460 --> 00:23:13.130
So what's this partnership
with Google all about?

00:23:13.130 --> 00:23:16.160
And obviously, we are
very excited about this,

00:23:16.160 --> 00:23:19.710
otherwise I would
not be here on stage.

00:23:19.710 --> 00:23:22.250
The scalability topic is
one of the major issues.

00:23:22.250 --> 00:23:24.975
Coming back to the example
I mentioned earlier, we

00:23:24.975 --> 00:23:28.075
are having these huge campaigns
running in these big countries,

00:23:28.075 --> 00:23:29.450
and we are also
serving countries

00:23:29.450 --> 00:23:33.260
like India and Pakistan,
just to bring you example.

00:23:33.260 --> 00:23:36.420
And therefore, scalability
is a massive topic for us.

00:23:36.420 --> 00:23:38.480
We are very happy about
the unmatched performance

00:23:38.480 --> 00:23:41.150
of the Google network
because we serve, as I said,

00:23:41.150 --> 00:23:43.820
customers globally,
and security is also

00:23:43.820 --> 00:23:45.770
very well covered by Google.

00:23:45.770 --> 00:23:47.960
And I know that Google
had a pretty hard time

00:23:47.960 --> 00:23:51.980
with our legal people,
with our governance people,

00:23:51.980 --> 00:23:54.050
and they did very well,
because at the end

00:23:54.050 --> 00:23:56.570
we managed to finally sign
a contract with Google

00:23:56.570 --> 00:23:59.520
and are now able to roll out
Google for our digital business

00:23:59.520 --> 00:24:02.900
worldwide, and be using the
Google Cloud Platform to make

00:24:02.900 --> 00:24:05.240
sure that our customers
get excellent service out

00:24:05.240 --> 00:24:07.554
of our platform.

00:24:07.554 --> 00:24:09.220
The other thing we
are doing with Google

00:24:09.220 --> 00:24:10.261
is obviously engineering.

00:24:10.261 --> 00:24:12.940
As I said, we have a huge
development community

00:24:12.940 --> 00:24:14.070
with our own organization.

00:24:14.070 --> 00:24:18.000
This is actually one of the
teams from us in Dusseldorf.

00:24:18.000 --> 00:24:22.600
And we are just exchanging with
Google how methodology works.

00:24:22.600 --> 00:24:24.100
For example, design
thinking is one

00:24:24.100 --> 00:24:26.380
of the major topics we are
currently investing in,

00:24:26.380 --> 00:24:29.740
but we are also leveraging
for our own applications

00:24:29.740 --> 00:24:31.240
the APIs provided by Google.

00:24:31.240 --> 00:24:33.550
So machine learning
is relevant for us.

00:24:33.550 --> 00:24:38.350
We're doing a lot of natural
language processing, voice

00:24:38.350 --> 00:24:39.950
recognition, image recognition.

00:24:39.950 --> 00:24:42.520
So we are pretty
well on this route,

00:24:42.520 --> 00:24:45.700
and therefore, using Google
as a technology partner

00:24:45.700 --> 00:24:50.180
is really essential for us also
to drive our own applications.

00:24:50.180 --> 00:24:52.500
So, and this is
obviously also something

00:24:52.500 --> 00:24:56.070
that's relevant for us,
innovation drives us massively.

00:24:56.070 --> 00:24:59.240
And we now have
obviously use cases

00:24:59.240 --> 00:25:02.400
like you see here on the
screen, where we just

00:25:02.400 --> 00:25:04.079
provide to our
customers, services

00:25:04.079 --> 00:25:06.120
based on Google technology,
such as we mentioned,

00:25:06.120 --> 00:25:08.250
there's a chef.

00:25:08.250 --> 00:25:12.120
Obviously, dirty hands cannot
type on computer or any tablet,

00:25:12.120 --> 00:25:14.940
so we offer them services
like, based on Google Home,

00:25:14.940 --> 00:25:18.330
so that they can order
Metro products directly out

00:25:18.330 --> 00:25:19.145
of the kitchen.

00:25:19.145 --> 00:25:21.270
So these are the kind of
services we are providing.

00:25:21.270 --> 00:25:23.430
So very happy to be
a part of Google.

00:25:23.430 --> 00:25:25.510
Enjoy the collaboration
very much,

00:25:25.510 --> 00:25:28.020
and thank you for
your attention.

00:25:28.020 --> 00:25:31.239
And have a wonderful
Google Cloud Summit today.

00:25:31.239 --> 00:25:33.704
