01:36:59.950 --> 01:37:04.030
And we've also had the chance
to, frankly, make some mistakes

01:37:04.030 --> 01:37:07.040
that, really, few
could afford to make.

01:37:07.040 --> 01:37:09.800
And that's what we want to
bring to this partnership.

01:37:09.800 --> 01:37:12.470
We want to bring and we
want to share that learning.

01:37:12.470 --> 01:37:14.835
We want to share
that experience.

01:37:18.146 --> 01:37:20.550
At Google, we have a saying.

01:37:20.550 --> 01:37:24.460
Focus on the user, and
all else will follow.

01:37:24.460 --> 01:37:28.170
We want to build a platform
that focuses on you.

01:37:28.170 --> 01:37:30.540
We want to build a
platform that's flexible,

01:37:30.540 --> 01:37:32.580
a platform that's open.

01:37:32.580 --> 01:37:36.630
We want to build a platform
that has easy to understand,

01:37:36.630 --> 01:37:39.540
customer friendly billing.

01:37:39.540 --> 01:37:44.670
We want to build a platform that
enables you to build and to run

01:37:44.670 --> 01:37:46.920
the applications
you want to run,

01:37:46.920 --> 01:37:50.800
but also the applications
that you need to run.

01:37:50.800 --> 01:37:53.650
We want to put you in
control of your IT.

01:37:57.010 --> 01:38:00.170
To give you some examples
of how we're doing that,

01:38:00.170 --> 01:38:03.390
I want to talk about our
sustained usage billing.

01:38:03.390 --> 01:38:06.080
So sustained usage
discounts is a scheme

01:38:06.080 --> 01:38:09.050
whereby the more you
use of our Cloud,

01:38:09.050 --> 01:38:12.470
the less we charge you per unit.

01:38:12.470 --> 01:38:15.280
We want to make billing simple.

01:38:15.280 --> 01:38:18.220
And so with sustained
usage discounts,

01:38:18.220 --> 01:38:20.450
those discounts are
applied automatically.

01:38:20.450 --> 01:38:23.080
You don't have to do anything.

01:38:23.080 --> 01:38:25.350
You just use the Cloud,
and we automatically

01:38:25.350 --> 01:38:27.300
work out what you
should be discounted,

01:38:27.300 --> 01:38:29.520
and we apply that
discount on your behalf,

01:38:29.520 --> 01:38:33.470
without you needing
to lift a finger.

01:38:33.470 --> 01:38:36.360
We also want to
make it flexible.

01:38:36.360 --> 01:38:38.670
So we offer that
sustained usage discount

01:38:38.670 --> 01:38:42.240
without any kind of commitment
upfront on your part,

01:38:42.240 --> 01:38:44.920
whatsoever.

01:38:44.920 --> 01:38:47.170
So it's a simple,
it's a flexible,

01:38:47.170 --> 01:38:52.330
it's a customer centric
model for billing, we feel.

01:38:52.330 --> 01:38:54.690
We're also extremely
committed to openness

01:38:54.690 --> 01:38:57.500
and to open standards.

01:38:57.500 --> 01:38:59.720
Google as a company was
born on the internet,

01:38:59.720 --> 01:39:01.760
and the internet was
born of open standards,

01:39:01.760 --> 01:39:07.040
and it's thrived as a result.
We are deeply, deeply committed

01:39:07.040 --> 01:39:09.890
to openness, and we're
deeply committed to allowing

01:39:09.890 --> 01:39:12.780
you to avoid vendor lock-in.

01:39:12.780 --> 01:39:16.690
Vendor lock-in kills innovation.

01:39:16.690 --> 01:39:19.150
Vendor lock-in kills innovation
because it doesn't allow

01:39:19.150 --> 01:39:21.238
the best technologies to win.

01:39:24.160 --> 01:39:27.880
And lastly, people.

01:39:27.880 --> 01:39:31.330
As I said before, we have
some amazing people in Google,

01:39:31.330 --> 01:39:33.940
and some amazing people that
really have the chance to build

01:39:33.940 --> 01:39:35.990
some really amazing things.

01:39:35.990 --> 01:39:38.350
And we want to bring
these people to you.

01:39:38.350 --> 01:39:40.600
We want you to work
together with these people

01:39:40.600 --> 01:39:44.434
to build the next generation
of crazy cool stuff

01:39:44.434 --> 01:39:45.358
on the internet.

01:39:49.060 --> 01:39:52.110
And you might say, that's great.

01:39:52.110 --> 01:39:55.624
Crazy, cool, I love it.

01:39:55.624 --> 01:39:57.040
That's kind of
cool, that's great.

01:39:57.040 --> 01:39:58.180
But come on, Tom.

01:39:58.180 --> 01:40:00.990
What about everything else?

01:40:00.990 --> 01:40:03.780
We understand we need
to run that as well.

01:40:03.780 --> 01:40:06.910
We need to make it easy
to bring new stuff,

01:40:06.910 --> 01:40:09.600
but we also need to make it easy
for you to bring your existing

01:40:09.600 --> 01:40:13.230
applications and your existing
investments onto our Cloud

01:40:13.230 --> 01:40:15.380
as well.

01:40:15.380 --> 01:40:19.130
Globally, CIOs are moving
to the Cloud to save money,

01:40:19.130 --> 01:40:21.830
but they're coming
and they're finding

01:40:21.830 --> 01:40:25.580
better security, better
reliability, better

01:40:25.580 --> 01:40:28.030
flexibility.

01:40:28.030 --> 01:40:31.000
We need to make it easy for
you to bring those applications

01:40:31.000 --> 01:40:32.555
to our Cloud.

01:40:32.555 --> 01:40:34.180
But we also want to
make sure that when

01:40:34.180 --> 01:40:36.320
you bring those
applications to the Cloud,

01:40:36.320 --> 01:40:40.780
we also make it easy for
you to migrate and to also

01:40:40.780 --> 01:40:43.510
take advantage of the new
services that you find there,

01:40:43.510 --> 01:40:46.870
services like the DLP,
the data loss prevention

01:40:46.870 --> 01:40:51.400
API, services like
Cloud Spanner.

01:40:51.400 --> 01:40:56.904
We want to enable you to
migrate and then to modernize.

01:40:56.904 --> 01:40:58.320
And we know that
we need to invest

01:40:58.320 --> 01:41:01.320
in the people, and the
processes, and the tools

01:41:01.320 --> 01:41:03.870
to allow you to do that.

01:41:03.870 --> 01:41:06.220
And one example of that is
our support for Windows.

01:41:08.730 --> 01:41:12.240
I hope here everybody
would accept and agree

01:41:12.240 --> 01:41:14.940
that our platform is an
amazing place to run Linux.

01:41:14.940 --> 01:41:18.780
It's an amazing place to
run Open Source workloads.

01:41:18.780 --> 01:41:22.160
There's also a lot of
Windows out there, right?

01:41:22.160 --> 01:41:25.020
We need to enable people
to run that as well.

01:41:25.020 --> 01:41:27.110
So we've made
investments in things

01:41:27.110 --> 01:41:30.530
like supporting images
for Windows server.

01:41:30.530 --> 01:41:32.380
Many different flavors
of Windows Server,

01:41:32.380 --> 01:41:36.530
many different flavors of SQL
server as standard images.

01:41:36.530 --> 01:41:39.200
We support hosting
Active Directory,

01:41:39.200 --> 01:41:42.440
so that you can extend your own
Premise Active Directory domain

01:41:42.440 --> 01:41:46.650
controller, into the Cloud.

01:41:46.650 --> 01:41:49.210
For Windows developers,
we want to be

01:41:49.210 --> 01:41:51.790
able to use the same,
familiar, powerful tools

01:41:51.790 --> 01:41:53.500
that you're used to using.

01:41:53.500 --> 01:41:56.440
So then we now
support Visual Studio.

01:41:56.440 --> 01:41:59.090
You can develop your
applications in Visual Studio,

01:41:59.090 --> 01:42:02.940
and you can easily
deploy them to our Cloud.

01:42:02.940 --> 01:42:07.630
The Cloud SDK supports over
100 different commandlets

01:42:07.630 --> 01:42:09.880
for the Windows
Power Shell to enable

01:42:09.880 --> 01:42:12.772
to use the tools that
you're familiar with to work

01:42:12.772 --> 01:42:14.716
in our environment.

01:42:18.610 --> 01:42:22.210
And one of the areas we've
made the biggest investment

01:42:22.210 --> 01:42:22.900
is in people.

01:42:25.680 --> 01:42:30.120
We know we need to bring
people to this partnership

01:42:30.120 --> 01:42:32.550
to help you to be successful.

01:42:32.550 --> 01:42:36.180
People like our customer
engineering and our solution

01:42:36.180 --> 01:42:38.820
architecture teams,
experts who can

01:42:38.820 --> 01:42:41.070
work with you to
build, and to design,

01:42:41.070 --> 01:42:44.500
and architect your applications
to get the best out

01:42:44.500 --> 01:42:46.640
of our Cloud.

01:42:46.640 --> 01:42:49.040
People like the
amazing engineers

01:42:49.040 --> 01:42:52.280
who sit in our
support organization.

01:42:52.280 --> 01:42:57.470
First class Google engineers,
who enjoy deep relationships

01:42:57.470 --> 01:42:59.600
with our software
engineering and our site

01:42:59.600 --> 01:43:02.885
reliability engineering teams,
so that when things go wrong,

01:43:02.885 --> 01:43:05.810
and things will occasionally
go wrong, we can get you up

01:43:05.810 --> 01:43:10.240
and running as fast
as we possibly can.

01:43:10.240 --> 01:43:14.140
People like our
office at the CTO.

01:43:14.140 --> 01:43:18.310
Seasoned industry professionals
with deep technical expertise

01:43:18.310 --> 01:43:20.890
and a background in
different verticals,

01:43:20.890 --> 01:43:22.900
who can work with customers
who are doing some

01:43:22.900 --> 01:43:27.190
of the largest, most audacious
migrations to the Cloud,

01:43:27.190 --> 01:43:31.000
migrations where deep technical
expertise and domain expertise

01:43:31.000 --> 01:43:35.300
are vital to be successful.

01:43:35.300 --> 01:43:39.080
People like our customer
liability engineers,

01:43:39.080 --> 01:43:41.660
taking the lessons we've
learned with site reliability

01:43:41.660 --> 01:43:45.950
engineering, running those
1 billion user applications,

01:43:45.950 --> 01:43:48.780
keeping those up and
running on the internet.

01:43:48.780 --> 01:43:50.880
People who can work
with you to bring

01:43:50.880 --> 01:43:55.410
the same level of resilience and
security to your applications

01:43:55.410 --> 01:43:58.560
so that you can build
applications that stay secure,

01:43:58.560 --> 01:44:01.890
that stay scalable, that
stay available under the most

01:44:01.890 --> 01:44:05.120
extreme of conditions.

01:44:05.120 --> 01:44:08.050
And lastly, Open Source.

01:44:08.050 --> 01:44:10.120
We have a lot of experience
with Open Source,

01:44:10.120 --> 01:44:11.740
and we can leverage
that experience

01:44:11.740 --> 01:44:14.380
to help you with your
Open Source packages,

01:44:14.380 --> 01:44:19.980
be that on our Cloud,
or be that on Premise.

01:44:19.980 --> 01:44:21.630
So to finish, I
just wanted to talk

01:44:21.630 --> 01:44:23.250
through an example of this.

01:44:23.250 --> 01:44:26.900
And a great example
of this is Conrad.

01:44:26.900 --> 01:44:30.320
Conrad's a 90-year-old
family owned company.

01:44:30.320 --> 01:44:33.830
And about 20 years ago, they
made a very smart investment,

01:44:33.830 --> 01:44:36.530
and they started to
invest in E-commerce.

01:44:36.530 --> 01:44:38.990
And today, Conrad is one
of the leading electronics

01:44:38.990 --> 01:44:41.610
suppliers both in
physical stores,

01:44:41.610 --> 01:44:45.010
but also on the internet.

01:44:45.010 --> 01:44:46.860
They are now working
with Google to move

01:44:46.860 --> 01:44:50.460
more and more of those
systems into our Cloud.

01:44:50.460 --> 01:44:54.060
Their IoT platform runs on
Google's Cloud and integrates

01:44:54.060 --> 01:44:57.150
with Google Assist.

01:44:57.150 --> 01:45:00.210
They have moved 5,000
of their employees

01:45:00.210 --> 01:45:03.930
to our G Suite platform to allow
them to better collaborate,

01:45:03.930 --> 01:45:07.260
to allow them to be empowered.

01:45:07.260 --> 01:45:09.866
And they save 90% of
people work in the process,

01:45:09.866 --> 01:45:10.740
which is pretty cool.

01:45:13.260 --> 01:45:15.270
But lastly, and most
importantly of all,

01:45:15.270 --> 01:45:16.950
they're working in
collaboration with us

01:45:16.950 --> 01:45:22.160
to explore new business models,
to explore new possibilities,

01:45:22.160 --> 01:45:23.870
and to test out the
bleeding edge of what

01:45:23.870 --> 01:45:26.052
we are making available.

01:45:26.052 --> 01:45:28.260
And I would urge you to go
and check out their booth.

01:45:28.260 --> 01:45:29.884
They have a very cool
booth downstairs,

01:45:29.884 --> 01:45:32.680
so go say hi to the
folks from Conrad

01:45:32.680 --> 01:45:36.780
and hear a little bit more
about their IoT platform.

01:45:36.780 --> 01:45:39.520
So in that, I hope
I've given you

01:45:39.520 --> 01:45:41.260
a bit of a flavor
of how we're working

01:45:41.260 --> 01:45:44.080
in partnership with you, how
we believe in openness, how

01:45:44.080 --> 01:45:48.360
we believe in bringing people
and bringing our expertise.

01:45:48.360 --> 01:45:50.430
I think it's an
extremely exciting time

01:45:50.430 --> 01:45:52.170
to be a technologist.

01:45:52.170 --> 01:45:53.800
I'm excited.

01:45:53.800 --> 01:45:56.159
I hope you're all excited, too.

01:45:56.159 --> 01:45:58.200
And with that, I'm going
to hand back to Michael.

01:45:58.200 --> 01:45:59.637
Thank you.

01:45:59.637 --> 01:46:03.739
[APPLAUSE]

01:46:03.739 --> 01:46:05.155
MICHAEL KORBACHER:
Thank you, Tom.

01:46:08.270 --> 01:46:08.890
Thank you.

01:46:11.920 --> 01:46:16.420
Yeah, so we spent the
last hour and a half

01:46:16.420 --> 01:46:20.010
on talking about four subjects,
four very important subjects,

01:46:20.010 --> 01:46:27.700
on your journey in
making the digital move.

01:46:27.700 --> 01:46:28.420
Optimize.

01:46:28.420 --> 01:46:31.630
Focus on the things
that differentiate you.

01:46:31.630 --> 01:46:36.580
Get rid of some of the
things that you shouldn't do.

01:46:36.580 --> 01:46:37.360
Collaborate.

01:46:37.360 --> 01:46:38.650
I think that's pretty obvious.

01:46:38.650 --> 01:46:42.580
We want to make sure we get
more productive, work better

01:46:42.580 --> 01:46:44.120
together.

01:46:44.120 --> 01:46:49.800
Engage and innovate and look
at the things of the future.

01:46:49.800 --> 01:46:52.260
Accelerate.

01:46:52.260 --> 01:46:58.130
Look at things like complex data
analytics, machine learning,

01:46:58.130 --> 01:47:03.282
and AI, and do that with
a partner that cares.

01:47:06.060 --> 01:47:10.265
The future of the Cloud is now.

01:47:13.080 --> 01:47:20.090
It's not if, it's
when, and when is now.

01:47:20.090 --> 01:47:22.940
I want to leave you with
an overview of what you

01:47:22.940 --> 01:47:25.610
can experience this afternoon.

01:47:25.610 --> 01:47:27.590
There are going to be
many sessions in four

01:47:27.590 --> 01:47:31.510
different tracks, and
you're ready to choose.

01:47:31.510 --> 01:47:36.230
There will be plenty of booths
outside from out of partners,

01:47:36.230 --> 01:47:39.380
as well as a start-up
booth out there,

01:47:39.380 --> 01:47:42.920
as well as a booth that says
ask an architect, where you'll

01:47:42.920 --> 01:47:45.020
meet with some of
our technical experts

01:47:45.020 --> 01:47:48.390
and you can talk
through architectures.

01:47:48.390 --> 01:47:50.110
Some of you have
already started.

01:47:50.110 --> 01:47:52.860
I've been curious
to share experience

01:47:52.860 --> 01:47:57.680
on the hashtag Google
Summit, Munich.

01:47:57.680 --> 01:48:00.230
And I want to leave you
with a little assignment

01:48:00.230 --> 01:48:03.380
for the afternoon.

01:48:03.380 --> 01:48:05.380
Take one of the
opportunities you

01:48:05.380 --> 01:48:07.120
have in mind, one
of the business

01:48:07.120 --> 01:48:11.740
opportunities you have in
mind, and take this opportunity

01:48:11.740 --> 01:48:18.460
with you into the sessions that
you'll follow this afternoon.

01:48:18.460 --> 01:48:23.050
And think about, how does this
session and what I'm hearing,

01:48:23.050 --> 01:48:27.330
how does that apply
to my opportunity?

01:48:27.330 --> 01:48:30.860
And make sure you
walk out of here today

01:48:30.860 --> 01:48:33.770
with something that
you're going to do

01:48:33.770 --> 01:48:37.850
different tomorrow that
is going to help you

01:48:37.850 --> 01:48:41.630
in fulfilling this idea.

01:48:41.630 --> 01:48:45.460
That said, I release
you into the afternoon,

01:48:45.460 --> 01:48:48.670
and I look forward
to seeing you again

01:48:48.670 --> 01:48:52.090
at our cocktail
reception at 6:15.

01:48:52.090 --> 01:48:53.020
Thank you.

01:48:53.020 --> 01:48:54.820
[APPLAUSE]

01:48:54.820 --> 01:48:58.170
